# TypeScript/JS sources are always text.
#
# `design-system/serializer.ts` carried a literal NUL byte (a delimiter written as
# a raw byte rather than an escape) until 0.2.9, and git therefore classified the
# whole file as binary: its diffs rendered as `Bin <n> -> <m> bytes` with no
# reviewable content, and grep skipped it silently. The byte is gone, but the
# next one should not be able to cost a reviewer a diff.
*.ts  text
*.tsx text
*.js  text
*.jsx text
*.mjs text
*.cjs text
*.json text
*.md  text
